===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|schade}}, from {{inh|de|goh|scado}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*skaþō}}. Confer {{cog|nl|schade}}, {{cog|en|scathe}}, {{cog|sv|skada}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃaː.d(ə)n/}}
* {{audio|de|De-schaden.ogg|audio}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schaden.oga|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Schadens|Schäden}}

# [[damage]]; [[harm]]
#: {{ux|de|Das Auto hat einen '''Schaden.'''|The car is damaged.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er hat seiner Frau nie '''Schaden''' zugefügt.|He has never done any harm to his wife.}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial|informal}} [[mental]] [[problem]] {{qualifier|in the sense of “crazy”}}
#: {{ux|de|Der hat doch ’n '''Schaden.'''|He must be out of his mind.}}

